**Definition 25.1 (bounded retry alternation).** Let $D(u)$ be the number of maximal nonempty $X$ blocks in the retry word $u$. Equivalently it is the number of distinct preceding-$Y$ counts at its $X$ occurrences. For an integer $d\ge0$ fixed publicly, define $\mathcal H_3^{[d]}(\mu)=\{h\in\mathcal H_3(\mu):D(u(h))\le d\}$. This promise parameter is distinct from the unchanged original source parameter $d=1$. It is an analysis promise, with both seeds, all marker triples, unbounded retry block lengths and unbounded returns. It supplies no segment signature, acquired retry archive or new source action.

